course: dictionary
lesson: 15083
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Ripped is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Her jeans were ripped at the knee.» The jeans have a tear, so ripped means torn here. Try the meaning in the sentence: "Her jeans were torn at the knee." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Sam ripped open the parcel to see his present.» Here ripped is the past form of the action word rip. It tells you what Sam did, and it happened in the past. Rip, rips and ripping are the other forms of the same verb.
explain: «We got ripped off at the market, because the toy cost far too much.» Ripped off is slang. It means cheated, or charged too much. The clue is the word "cost": the price was too high.
fact: Ripped can be an adjective, meaning torn, or the past form of the verb rip.
fact: «Ripped» means torn, often roughly or suddenly, as in «ripped jeans».
fact: «Ripped off» means cheated or charged too much. It is informal, so use it in talk, not in formal writing.
fact: «Ripped» can also be slang for having very strong, clearly seen muscles, as in «he's ripped».
fact: Ripped out means pulled out by force, as in «the old fence was ripped out».
exercise: «The old fence was ripped out by the storm.» What does ripped out mean? | Counted in pieces | Fixed carefully | Painted bright red | *Pulled out by force
exercise: «We got ripped off at the shop, because the toy cost far too much.» What does ripped off mean here? | *Cheated or charged too much | Lost on the way home | Wrapped up nicely | Given a free gift
exercise: «Ali ripped the paper off the box.» Which form of rip is ripped in this sentence? | *The past form of the verb rip | The plural of rip | A name for a type of paper | The present form of rip
test: «Her ripped jeans are very popular this year.» In this sentence, what does ripped mean? | Strong | Cheated | Pulled out | *Torn
test: «Max has been training all summer, and now he is ripped.» What does ripped mean here? | Torn into pieces | Charged too much | Hungry | *Having very strong, clearly seen muscles
exam: «The paper was ripped into eight pieces, so each child got two.» What does ripped mean in this sentence? | *Torn into pieces | Pulled out by force | Cheated out of a prize | Strong and fit
